    "quote": "Let $\\{f_t\\}_{t=1}^T$ be a sequence of $M_1$-Lipschitz non-monotone DR-submodular functions. Instantiating base learner to be SO-OGA as described in Algorithm~\\ref{alg:so_oga_base}, Algorithm \\ref{alg:main} achieves a $1/e$-approximation static regret bounded by: \\E[ \\alpha \\max_{\\bu \\in \\mathcal{K}}\\sum_{t=1}^T f_t(\\bu) - \\sum_{t=1}^T f_t(\\hbx_t) ] \\le \\CO(M_1 \\sqrt{T}). The algorithm requires only $\\CO(1)$ gradient queries per round."
